# Backend routes intentionally not called by any frontend.
#
# The route-usage gate (test/routes.test.mjs) fails the build when a registered
# route has no caller in the passport app or the admin console. A route that is
# server-only or operator-only by design belongs here so the gate stays green.
#
# One entry per line:  METHOD /template   reason it is not frontend-called
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored. A reason is required.
#
# Prefer DELETING an unused route (and its handler + tests) over listing it here.
# An entry is checked both ways: if its route stops being registered, or starts
# being frontend-called, the gate fails until the entry is removed.

GET /{$}                           public landing HTML served to browsers, never an API call
GET /admin/errors                  console panel lands in the next PR, which removes this entry
GET /admin/perf                    console panel lands in the next PR, which removes this entry
POST /admin/errors/clear           console control lands in the next PR, which removes this entry
